  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Fractions of amounts"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is a fraction?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- A fraction is written as $\\frac{a}{b}$ where *a* and *b* are** *****integers***\n\n  - The number on the top, *a*, is called the **numerator**\n  - The number on the bottom, *b*, is called the **denominator**\n- The **values** of the numerator and denominator tell us about the** size** of the fraction** **\n\n  - The denominator is how many **parts** each whole number is split into\n  - The numerator is how many** parts** you **have**\n  \n    - For example, $\\frac{2}{3}$ means that each whole number  is divided into 3 parts and you have 2 of these parts\n- A fraction is **less **than 1 if the numerator is **smaller **than the denominator\n- A fraction is **more **than 1 if the number is **bigger **than the denominator"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I shade a fraction on a diagram?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Divide** by the **denominator** and **multiply** by the **numerator**\n\n  - To shade $\\frac{3}{5}$ of a grid of 20 squares\n  \n    - **Divide** 20 squares by 5 to get 4 squares\n    - **Multiply** this amount by 3 to get 12 squares\n    - **Shade** 12 squares\n  - To shade $\\frac{1}{4}$ of a circle\n  \n    - **Divide** the circle into four quarters by drawing a horizontal and a vertical line through the centre\n    - **Shade** one of these quarters"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I find a fraction of an amount?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Method 1**\n**Divide** by the **denominator** and **multiply** by the **numerator**\n\n  - To find $\\frac{1}{3}$ of $90$, divide it by 3\n  \n    - $90\\div3=30$\n  - To find $\\frac{2}{5}$ of $60$, divide it by 5 then multiply it by 2\n  \n    - $60\\div5=12$, then $12\\times2=24$\n- **Method 2**\n**Multiply **the  amount by the fraction\n\n  - To find $\\frac{9}{10}$ of $15$, multiply them together\n  \n    - $\\frac{9}{10}\\times15=13.5$"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
   "md": "Shade $\\frac{5}{7}$ of the grid below.\n\n![grid 1](assets/268f6c388af7-11999-introduction-to-fractions.png)\n\n**Answer:**\n\n> *Count the total number of squares in the grid*\n\n*Total of 21 squares*\n\n> *Divide 21 by 7*\n\n* 21 ÷ 7 = 3*\n\n> *Multiply by 5*\n\n*3 × 5 = 15*\n\n> *Shade 15 squares *\n\n- * It doesn't matter which 15 you shade*\n- *It's neater to group them together*\n\n![grid 2](assets/ef782e8fef85-3879-introduction-to-fractions-2.png)"
  }
 ]
